1
00:00:21,517 --> 00:00:22,577
Run your agents.

2
00:00:22,627 --> 00:00:23,617
Check the math.

3
00:00:25,717 --> 00:00:28,136
Every company running AI agents can see two things.

4
00:00:28,186 --> 00:00:31,427
How many seats they bought, and how many tokens those agents burned.

5
00:00:31,477 --> 00:00:35,542
What they cannot see is whether the work the agents said they did, they actually did.

6
00:00:36,717 --> 00:00:38,047
An agent writes a sentence.

7
00:00:38,097 --> 00:00:39,120
Committed as deadbee.

8
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:44,842
Nothing checks that sentence against the repository, and at fleet scale, that sentence is what auto-merge reads.

9
00:00:46,517 --> 00:00:47,219
So we check it.

10
00:00:47,269 --> 00:00:51,581
The gate takes the claim, turns it into a probe, and runs the probe against the object.

11
00:00:51,631 --> 00:00:52,233
Git cat file.

12
00:00:52,283 --> 00:00:53,386
Does that commit exist.

13
00:00:53,436 --> 00:00:55,592
It does not, so the pull request is blocked.

14
00:00:56,717 --> 00:00:59,252
A check that only ever says no is not a check.

15
00:00:59,302 --> 00:01:00,657
Here is an honest report.

16
00:01:00,707 --> 00:01:02,792
Real commit, real file, and it passes.

17
00:01:04,217 --> 00:01:06,306
And here is the one it refuses to guess at.

18
00:01:06,356 --> 00:01:07,401
The commit checks out.

19
00:01:07,451 --> 00:01:12,873
All fourteen tests pass does not, because verifying that would mean running a command lifted from agent prose.

20
00:01:12,923 --> 00:01:14,067
It is held, not guessed.

21
00:01:15,717 --> 00:01:17,734
The backend is live on Google Cloud Run.

22
00:01:17,784 --> 00:01:20,627
This is the deployed service, its URL, and its revision.

23
00:01:20,677 --> 00:01:22,022
Firestore holds the record.

24
00:01:22,072 --> 00:01:26,104
Gemini three point five, through the Agent Development Kit, explains a verdict.

25
00:01:26,154 --> 00:01:27,292
It never overrules one.

26
00:01:29,217 --> 00:01:30,785
And eligibility is not an import.

27
00:01:30,835 --> 00:01:33,922
This script calls all three services rather than importing them.

28
00:01:33,972 --> 00:01:36,717
With credentials it prints three of three and exits zero.

29
00:01:36,767 --> 00:01:42,992
Cold, with no credentials, it prints one of three and exits one, deliberately, because a class name proves an import, not a run.

30
00:01:49,217 --> 00:01:51,917
And here is that same service in the Google Cloud console.

31
00:01:51,967 --> 00:01:54,477
Cloud Run, us central one, healthy, scaling from zero.

32
00:01:54,527 --> 00:02:01,161
The request graph is live, and the logs underneath it are this recording's own traffic arriving at the deployed service, timestamped tonight.

33
00:02:01,211 --> 00:02:03,959
Firestore holds every clearance as an append only document.

34
00:02:04,009 --> 00:02:06,092
None of this is a screenshot of an intention.

35
00:02:07,217 --> 00:02:11,046
This is the Agent Work Record Witness, and the gate is only its intake.

36
00:02:11,096 --> 00:02:12,467
The record is the product.

37
00:02:14,717 --> 00:02:18,649
Before we pointed this at anyone else, we pointed it at a month of our own agent output.

38
00:02:18,699 --> 00:02:22,495
It said forty one point seven percent of commit claims disagreed with the repository.

39
00:02:22,545 --> 00:02:24,576
That number was wrong, and the error was ours.

40
00:02:24,626 --> 00:02:28,920
Seventy three of a hundred and three were real commits in a sibling repository on the same disk.

41
00:02:28,970 --> 00:02:31,092
The corrected figure is eight point one percent.

42
00:02:31,717 --> 00:02:33,082
Here is a held claim, opened.

43
00:02:33,132 --> 00:02:36,058
It resolves all the way back to the session that produced it.

44
00:02:36,108 --> 00:02:42,792
That join is the thing no observability tool, no code reviewer and no compliance product holds, because none of them keeps the transcript.

45
00:02:43,517 --> 00:02:46,953
Every Google service on the request path, with the probe that shows it.

46
00:02:47,003 --> 00:02:49,309
The queue humans actually open, calm by default.

47
00:02:49,359 --> 00:02:51,273
And the record, exportable, append only.

48
00:02:51,323 --> 00:02:52,304
Zero percent cleared.

49
00:02:52,354 --> 00:02:55,642
Nothing has passed, and that is the honest state, not a broken demo.

50
00:03:00,717 --> 00:03:03,278
Installing it is a policy URL and one GitHub action.

51
00:03:03,328 --> 00:03:06,943
The probe runs inside your own checkout, where the repository already is.

52
00:03:06,993 --> 00:03:12,517
Only the verdict and a session pointer cross the network, so this product never needs read access to your code.

53
00:03:13,217 --> 00:03:14,424
The policy is explicit.

54
00:03:14,474 --> 00:03:21,092
Enforce mode, scoped to pull requests an agent actually opened, with a named break-glass role for the human who overrides.

55
00:03:21,717 --> 00:03:24,406
One real agent pull request went through the gate.

56
00:03:24,456 --> 00:03:25,665
Verify claims went red.

57
00:03:25,715 --> 00:03:27,692
It failed on purpose, and it is held.

58
00:03:29,217 --> 00:03:31,753
What is next is the half we are asking for help with.

59
00:03:31,803 --> 00:03:33,461
Separating a citation from a claim.

60
00:03:33,511 --> 00:03:36,243
Committed as X, and commit X landed, are the same string.

61
00:03:36,293 --> 00:03:37,609
Only the speech act differs.

62
00:03:37,659 --> 00:03:41,367
And the thing we do not have yet: a single install by somebody who is not us.

63
00:03:42,217 --> 00:03:43,950
The Agent Work Record Witness.

64
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:44,901
Run your agents.

65
00:03:44,951 --> 00:03:45,792
Check the math.
